{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NTEzMTIy","is_bot":false,"login":"tobias-tengler","name":"Tobias Tengler"},"baseRefOid":"9a563e814f3b6213c80a6bc96a01fbcb4d605096","body":"Fusion starts variable coercion with an empty dictionary, repeatedly allocating larger bucket and entry arrays as supplied variables are inserted.\n\nThis PR pre-sizes the dictionary from an allocation-free count of supplied properties, bounded by the variable-definition count and 256.\n\n### Benchmarks\n\nThe direct benchmark calls the real variable coercion helper with 200 nullable definitions and either one or all 200 values supplied. Definition and input-JSON parsing are outside the timed region.\n\nBenchmarkDotNet 0.15.8, Release .NET 10.0.12 ARM64, server/concurrent GC: three launches, five warmup iterations and fifteen measured iterations per launch. Values are medians after BDN outlier filtering; ratios are relative to the baseline. Baseline `main` is `9a563e814f`; the PR is `8644259a6a`.\n\nBoth variants use `DOTNET_GCDynamicAdaptationMode=0` for microbenchmarks and HTTP comparisons to avoid observed allocation-counter discontinuities. This is a measurement setting, not a production change; default-GC HTTP CPU/allocation effects are not independently established.\n\n| Case | Version | Median | Ratio | Allocated | Alloc Ratio |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 of 200 supplied | `main` | 5.324 µs | 1.00 | 400 B | 1.00 |\n| 1 of 200 supplied | PR | 5.428 µs | 1.02 | 400 B | 1.00 |\n| 200 of 200 supplied | `main` | 72.749 µs | 1.00 | 50,760 B | 1.00 |\n| 200 of 200 supplied | PR | 70.135 µs | 0.96 | 26,600 B | 0.52 |\n\nThe sparse case is 1.94% slower at the median (103 ns), with overlapping timing ranges and unchanged allocation. The fully supplied case saves 24,160 B/op (47.6%); timing ranges also overlap.\n\n### Verdict\n\nAt 100 requests/s, gateway allocation/request fell 10.35%, 17.13% and 22.06% for 50, 100 and 200 supplied variables. A fresh 200-variable pair reproduced a 22.10% reduction. This is a transient-allocation improvement; a stable gateway CPU improvement was not established, and the fixed offered rates do not establish higher throughput capacity.\n\nRelease builds passed; 30 focused tests passed. [Full results and reproduction](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/blob/8644259a6ad49f533f54851d565931551adb37ce/PERFORMANCE-variable-coercion.md).\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOBvrWZ88AAAABctz4Ag","author":{"login":"github-actions"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"## Patch coverage\n\n**100.0%** of changed lines covered (11/11)\n\n| File | Covered | Changed | Patch % |\n|:-----|--------:|--------:|--------:|\n| […/src/Fusion.Execution/Execution/VariableCoercionHelper.cs](https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10558/files#diff-f50b0823a3227741ad2eedb24d5d4bcadf56638ae28c0412a78a60e66139c1e4) | 11 | 11 | 100.0%&nbsp;🟢 |\n\n---\n\nProject coverage: **59.0%** (311293/527650 lines)\n\n\n<!-- Sticky Pull Request Commentpatch-coverage -->","createdAt":"2026-10-16T18:25:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ChilliCream/graphql-platform/pull/10558#issuecomment-6222051330","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"files":[{"path":"PERFORMANCE-variable-coercion.md","additions":130,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/Directory.Build.props","additions":10,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/README.md","additions":64,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/agg_speedscope.py","additions":57,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze.py","additions":102,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/analyze_profiles.py","additions":31,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"benchmarks/fusion-performance/audit.py","additions":84,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"ben